lly, a report from the Madison.com archive states that \"Donald Trump to hold rally in Waukesha on Saturday\" on October 23, 2020.", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Donald_Trump_rallies_(December_2016%E2%80%932022)", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Does the design of the flag displayed behind Donald Trump at the Waukesha rally correspond to known \"anti-Black Lives Matter\" iconography?", "answer": "Yes, the \"thin blue line\" symbol is used by the \"Blue Lives Matter\" movement, which \"emerged in 2014 as a rebuttal to the Black Lives Matter movement.\" Additionally, the search result notes that the \"thin blue line US flag has appeared regularly at Trump rallies.\"", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thin_blue_line", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Did the flag displayed behind Donald Trump at the Waukesha rally physically replace the position typically occupied by the American flag?", "answer": "The search result does not explicitly state whether the Thin Blue Line flag physically replaced the position of the American flag, but it notes that the flag was \"hung prominently behind the risers behind the podium where Trump spoke\" and that its use was \"a change from the last several Wisconsin rallies that Trump has held in other cities.\"", "url": "https://api.politifact.com/factchecks/2020/oct/28/facebook-posts/yes-thin-blue-line-flag-has-taken-more-prominent-p/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}], "justification": "During a Donald Trump campaign rally in Waukesha, Wisconsin, on October 23, 2020, a [thin blue line flag](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thin_blue_line) was hung prominently behind the podium, marking a change from previous rallies in other Wisconsin cities. The thin blue line symbol is associated with the [Blue Lives Matter movement](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thin_blue_line), which emerged as a rebuttal to the Black Lives Matter movement, and such flags have appeared regularly at Trump rallies. While the record notes the flag was positioned prominently behind the risers, [Politifact](https://api.politifact.com/factchecks/2020/oct/28/facebook-posts/yes-thin-blue-line-flag-has-taken-more-prominent-p/) confirms its prominent placement during the event.", "admitted_sources": [{"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Donald_Trump_rallies_(December_2016%E2%80%932022)", "date": "2017-03-19", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.c-span.org/program/white-house-event/president-trump-holds-rally-in-waukesha-wisconsin/555346", "date": "2020-10-24", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.wbay.com/2020/10/24/president-trump-to-hold-campaign-rally-in-waukesha-saturday-evening/", "date": "2020-10-24", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.c-span.org/program/white-house-event/president-trump-holds-rally-in-waukesha-wisconsin/555346", "date": "2020-10-24", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.gmtoday.com/news/trump-motivates-voters-at-rally-in-waukesha/article_2892d1e4-1672-11eb-ad98-63985d599b31.html", "date": "2020-10-24", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.newyorker.com/news/campaign-chronicles/will-trumps-law-and-order-message-work-in-wisconsins-white-suburbs", "date": "2020-10-24", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://marquettewire.org/3955414/tv/photos-trump-visits-waukesha/", "date": "2016-09-29", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.gmtoday.com/news/trump-motivates-voters-at-rally-in-waukesha/article_2892d1e4-1672-11eb-ad98-63985d59